KG42.register("rules-dc1dfda766c5b502164269c4",{"id":"32-wholesale_prosumer_storage::v141-c-R002","paper":"32-wholesale_prosumer_storage","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R002","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local market coordinator","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"STEP only coordinates system information flows and does not assume ownership of electricity. Scope: STEP interface coordinating information between the community and wholesale electricity markets. STEP makes automatic decisions based on rules specified by community members and is a computational interface without the role of a service providing agent. Scope: Automatic operation of the STEP computational interface between the wholesale market and the community. STEP aims to minimise expected costs for the community’s local market. Scope: STEP planning for the community’s local market and its day-ahead market decisions.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.local_operator under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.local_operator"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Automatic operation of the STEP computational interface between the wholesale market and the community. | STEP interface coordinating information between the community and wholesale electricity markets. | STEP planning for the community’s local market and its day-ahead market decisions.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g02-e08"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"STEP only coordinates system information flows and does not assume ownership of electricity. Scope: STEP interface coordinating information between the community and wholesale electricity markets.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e06"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"STEP makes automatic decisions based on rules specified by community members and is a computational interface without the role of a service providing agent. Scope: Automatic operation of the STEP computational interface between the wholesale market and the community.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e08"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"STEP aims to minimise expected costs for the community’s local market. Scope: STEP planning for the community’s local market and its day-ahead market decisions.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The STEP automatically performs the bidding into the day- ahead market based on the community’s dema","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The STEP automatically performs the bidding into the day-ahead market based on the community’s demand and day-ahead forecasted generation. The STEP is slightly different from aggregator models (see e.g. [33,34]) as it only coordinates the information flows (i.e. a smart box) in the system and does not assume ownership of the electricity. It then acts automatically based on this information, i.e. it bids to or procures electricity from the wholesale market, and plans the P2P trade and battery utilisation in the community. The STEP is not a service providing agent, but rather a computational interface between the wholesale market and the community which makes automatic decisions based on rules specified by the community members. Fig. 2 illustrates the flow of information between the markets and the role of the STEP."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e13","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"market. In this paper, the market design allows P2P trade among ec- prosumers and consumers in a com","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"For the integration of communities into the existing electricity markets, we propose a bidirectional connection from the local market to the main electricity markets. This entails a virtual connection allowing for trade, and physical connections of individual buildings with the main power grid. To jointly plan loads and charging in the local market as well as bidding and scheduling decisions in the day-ahead market, we introduce a Smart elecTricity Exchange Platform (STEP). This platform aims at minimising the expected costs for the community’s local market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e08","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The STEP automatically performs the bidding into the day- ahead market based on the community’s dema","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The STEP automatically performs the bidding into the day-ahead market based on the community’s demand and day-ahead forecasted generation. The STEP is slightly different from aggregator models (see e.g. [33,34]) as it only coordinates the information flows (i.e. a smart box) in the system and does not assume ownership of the electricity. It then acts automatically based on this information, i.e. it bids to or procures electricity from the wholesale market, and plans the P2P trade and battery utilisation in the community. The STEP is not a service providing agent, but rather a computational interface between the wholesale market and the community which makes automatic decisions based on rules specified by the community members."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"No x are declared because the frozen V contains only coordination.local_operator and the supplied evidence for this coordination rule describes the STEP interface's institutional role and information-coordination behavior, not a decision variable owned by the coordinator within this rule. Model decision variables are scoped to the bidding, clearing, and execution rules, not imported here.","empty_theta_reason":"No theta are declared because the supplied evidence for this rule gives no fixed numeric or symbolic parameter belonging to the coordination relation itself. Coefficients and fixed values mentioned elsewhere in the paper, such as loss factors or network charges, are not used by these three coordination statements and are not moved into this rule."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.local_operator","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e06","quote":"The STEP is slightly different from aggregator models (see e.g. [33,34]) as it only coordinates the information flows (i.e. a smart box) in the system and does not assume ownership of the electricity."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e08","quote":"The STEP is not a service providing agent, but rather a computational interface between the wholesale market and the community which makes automatic decisions based on rules specified by the community members."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e13","quote":"This platform aims at minimising the expected costs for the community’s local market."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"d23be812462b82292090083ea8f34c1909d53e201bda660ce77bbb3a1607a7df","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule contains only source-backed institutional/role characterizations of the STEP coordination function: it coordinates information flows, does not own electricity, acts as a computational interface rather than a service-providing agent, makes automatic decisions under community-specified rules, and has an expected-cost aim. The supplied B quotations for this rule provide no numerical or symbolic equation defining the coordinator itself. The model-wide objective and decision equations are outside this frozen unary coordination node's declared V/E scope, so no local optimization formula is invented here. The supplied B evidence remains unreviewed; no independent source verification is claimed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C001 characterizes the local operator node in unary procedural terms: STEP coordinates information flows and does not assume electricity ownership. The frozen graph supplies no edge for this non-ownership statement."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-C002","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C002 further characterizes the same local operator node as a computational interface making automatic decisions under community-specified rules and not acting as a service-providing agent. This is a unary role description in the frozen graph."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-C003","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C003 attributes an expected-cost objective aim to the local operator node. No objective expression is assigned because the frozen rule declares no variables, parameters, or graph edge through which the model-wide objective would be represented."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
